title: A reply typed in the unread list vanishes on save, and its message stays unread.
pid: 22a1ef4b-17e6-4d7b-8050-90508fccd820
body: |2-
  Steps, as Ed: in Jeff's inbox with the subscribee made editable, I
  typed a child under the 17:35 message, saved and approved the fork.
  The redraw showed the original, now '1S 1O', with no child; the count
  stayed 'C32/35'. The reply exists only as a fork no note contains.
  Not tested as Jeff: there the fork would be his own, the root's
  author's, and might stand in the message's place. His filing of his
  forks under 'maybe done' fits the reply vanishing for him too.
